{"id": "rf-001", "release": "2026_11", "case": "narrower_key", "errors": [{"pattern": "5J8TB3H3*EL", "model_year": 2014, "make": "ACURA", "model": "RDX", "field": "DriveType", "vpic_value": "AWD/All-Wheel Drive", "correct_value": "FWD", "test_vehicles": 2}], "edits": [{"action": "modify", "table": "pattern", "row": {"id": 845254, "schema_id": 9925, "schema": "Acura RDX Schema for 2014", "keys": "TB[34]H[35]", "element": "DriveType", "attribute_id": "3", "value": "AWD/All-Wheel Drive"}, "set": {"keys": "TB3H[35]", "attribute_id": "1", "value": "FWD/Front-Wheel Drive"}}], "reason": "Position 6 separates the drives: vPIC's own row TB4H[35] gives AWD, and both NHTSA test RDXs with TB3 were front-drive (EPA lists the 2014 RDX 2WD and 4WD). The row TB[34]H[35] gave AWD to both; it now covers TB3 only, as front-wheel drive.", "evidence": [{"url": "https://nrd-static.nhtsa.dot.gov/reports/vehdb/v00000/v08300/v08357R001.pdf", "test_no": 8357}, {"url": "https://nrd-static.nhtsa.dot.gov/reports/vehdb/v00000/v08300/v08359R001.pdf", "test_no": 8359}], "reviewed": {"on": "2026-11-18", "by": "mcp.vin decode audit 2026-11-17 (confirmed list); rule rows traced by the local decoder"}, "checks": [{"vin": "5J8TB3H35EL005547", "fields": {"DriveType": {"official_value": "AWD/All-Wheel Drive", "fixed_value": "FWD/Front-Wheel Drive"}}}, {"vin": "5J8TB3H37EL006151", "fields": {"DriveType": {"official_value": "AWD/All-Wheel Drive", "fixed_value": "FWD/Front-Wheel Drive"}}}]}
{"id": "rf-002", "release": "2026_11", "case": "narrower_key", "errors": [{"pattern": "3GN7DLRR*RS", "model_year": 2024, "make": "CHEVROLET", "model": "Equinox", "field": "DriveType", "vpic_value": "FWD/Front-Wheel Drive", "correct_value": "AWD/4WD", "test_vehicles": 1}], "edits": [{"action": "modify", "table": "pattern", "row": {"id": 1942055, "schema_id": 25558, "schema": "Chevrolet Equinox EV Schema for 3GN (MY2024)", "keys": "7D[8K-S]*[PR]", "element": "DriveType", "attribute_id": "1", "value": "FWD/Front-Wheel Drive"}, "set": {"keys": "7D[8K-S]*P"}}, {"action": "add", "table": "pattern", "new": {"id": -101, "schema_id": 25558, "schema": "Chevrolet Equinox EV Schema for 3GN (MY2024)", "keys": "7D[8K-S]*R", "element": "DriveType", "attribute_id": "3", "value": "AWD/All-Wheel Drive"}}], "reason": "Position 8 separates the drives: vPIC's own OtherEngineInfo rows read 'GEN 3, FWD, 10-MOD' for P and 'GEN 3, FWD, EAWD, 10-MOD' for R. The drive row 7D[8K-S]*[PR] gave front drive to both; it now covers P, and R gets all-wheel drive (NHTSA's AWD test Equinox EV has R; the two front-drive ones have P).", "evidence": [{"url": "https://nrd-static.nhtsa.dot.gov/reports/vehdb/v10000/v15000/v15092R001.pdf", "test_no": 15092}], "reviewed": {"on": "2026-11-18", "by": "mcp.vin decode audit 2026-11-17 (confirmed list); rule rows traced by the local decoder"}, "checks": [{"vin": "3GN7DLRR1RS241049", "fields": {"DriveType": {"official_value": "FWD/Front-Wheel Drive", "fixed_value": "AWD/All-Wheel Drive"}}}]}
{"id": "rf-003", "release": "2026_11", "case": "narrower_key", "errors": [{"pattern": "KMHM34AC*PA", "model_year": 2023, "make": "HYUNDAI", "model": "Ioniq 6", "field": "DriveType", "vpic_value": "RWD/Rear-Wheel Drive", "correct_value": "AWD/4WD", "test_vehicles": 1}], "edits": [{"action": "add", "table": "pattern", "new": {"id": -102, "schema_id": 24962, "schema": "Hyundai IONIQ 6 Schema for KMH (MY2023)", "keys": "M[235]4*C", "element": "DriveType", "attribute_id": "3", "value": "AWD/All-Wheel Drive"}}], "premise": [{"table": "spec_pattern", "row": {"id": 227577, "spec_schema_pattern_id": 12925, "spec_schema_id": 3567, "applies_to": "Ioniq 6 2023, where BodyClass=Sedan/Saloon", "element": "DriveType", "attribute_id": "4", "value": "RWD/Rear-Wheel Drive"}}], "reason": "vPIC's vehicle-spec row gives rear drive to every 2023 Ioniq 6 sedan, but EPA lists RWD and AWD versions. NHTSA's AWD test car has C at position 8, the two RWD ones A. A pattern row for C (all-wheel drive) now outranks the spec value; A and B keep vPIC's rear drive.", "evidence": [{"url": "https://nrd-static.nhtsa.dot.gov/reports/vehdb/v10000/v15000/v15029R001.pdf", "test_no": 15029}], "reviewed": {"on": "2026-11-18", "by": "mcp.vin decode audit 2026-11-17 (confirmed list); rule rows traced by the local decoder"}, "checks": [{"vin": "KMHM34AC7PA022456", "fields": {"DriveType": {"official_value": "RWD/Rear-Wheel Drive", "fixed_value": "AWD/All-Wheel Drive"}}}]}
{"id": "rf-004", "release": "2026_11", "case": "wrong_row", "errors": [{"pattern": "JN8AY2NC*J9", "model_year": 2018, "make": "NISSAN", "model": "Armada", "field": "DriveType", "vpic_value": "4x2", "correct_value": "AWD/4WD", "test_vehicles": 1}], "edits": [{"action": "delete", "table": "pattern", "row": {"id": 1249451, "schema_id": 15607, "schema": "Nissan/Infiniti MPV Schema for JN8/5N1/3N8/KNM - 2018", "keys": "AY2N", "element": "DriveType", "attribute_id": "7", "value": "4x2"}}], "reason": "The row AY2N (4x2 for every 2018 Armada) overrode vPIC's own position-8 drive rows, which give 4WD to C and 4x2 to D. NHTSA's test Armadas agree with position 8 (C: 4WD; D: rear drive). Removing the row lets the position-8 rows decide.", "evidence": [{"url": "https://nrd-static.nhtsa.dot.gov/reports/vehdb/v10000/v10300/v10312R001.pdf", "test_no": 10312}], "reviewed": {"on": "2026-11-18", "by": "mcp.vin decode audit 2026-11-17 (confirmed list); rule rows traced by the local decoder"}, "checks": [{"vin": "JN8AY2NC0J9555172", "fields": {"DriveType": {"official_value": "4x2", "fixed_value": "4WD/4-Wheel Drive/4x4"}}}]}
{"id": "rf-005", "release": "2026_11", "case": "narrower_key", "errors": [{"pattern": "JN8AF5MV*CT", "model_year": 2012, "make": "NISSAN", "model": "Juke", "field": "DriveType", "vpic_value": "4x2", "correct_value": "AWD/4WD", "test_vehicles": 1}], "edits": [{"action": "modify", "table": "pattern", "row": {"id": 58028, "schema_id": 2849, "schema": "Nissan/Infiniti MPV JN8/5N1 Schema - 2012", "keys": "****[B-FNPRT-WY]", "element": "DriveType", "attribute_id": "7", "value": "4x2"}, "set": {"keys": "****[DFNPRTU]"}}], "reason": "Two of vPIC's rows overlapped at position 8: ****[B-FNPRT-WY] (4x2) and ****[VWBCEY] (4WD) both covered B, C, E, V, W and Y, and the 4x2 row won. NHTSA's AWD test Juke has V and the front-drive ones R. The 4x2 row now leaves out the 4WD row's letters.", "evidence": [{"url": "https://nrd-static.nhtsa.dot.gov/reports/vehdb/v00000/v07600/v07626R001.pdf", "test_no": 7626}], "reviewed": {"on": "2026-11-18", "by": "mcp.vin decode audit 2026-11-17 (confirmed list); rule rows traced by the local decoder"}, "checks": [{"vin": "JN8AF5MV4CT106612", "fields": {"DriveType": {"official_value": "4x2", "fixed_value": "4WD/4-Wheel Drive/4x4"}}}]}
{"id": "rf-006", "release": "2026_11", "case": "wrong_value", "errors": [{"pattern": "5TDZA3EH*BS", "model_year": 2011, "make": "TOYOTA", "model": "Highlander", "field": "DriveType", "vpic_value": "4WD/4-Wheel Drive/4x4", "correct_value": "4x2", "test_vehicles": 1}], "edits": [{"action": "modify", "table": "pattern", "row": {"id": 85981, "schema_id": 3146, "schema": "Toyota Schema for Highlander/Highlander Limited/Highlander Hybrid/Highlander Hybrid Limited MPVs for JTE/5TD - 2011", "keys": "Z***H", "element": "DriveType", "attribute_id": "2", "value": "4WD/4-Wheel Drive/4x4"}, "set": {"attribute_id": "7", "value": "4x2"}}], "reason": "Position 4 encodes the drive in Toyota's 2011 rows (B and D: 4WD, Y: 4x2; the Sienna and Sequoia rows give Z 4x2), but Z***H said 4WD. NHTSA's test Highlander with Z was two-wheel drive, and EPA lists no 4WD Highlander with the decoded engine.", "evidence": [{"url": "https://nrd-static.nhtsa.dot.gov/reports/vehdb/v00000/v07100/v07181R001.pdf", "test_no": 7181}], "reviewed": {"on": "2026-11-18", "by": "mcp.vin decode audit 2026-11-17 (confirmed list); rule rows traced by the local decoder"}, "checks": [{"vin": "5TDZA3EH9BS009588", "fields": {"DriveType": {"official_value": "4WD/4-Wheel Drive/4x4", "fixed_value": "4x2"}}}, {"vin": "5TDZA3EH9BS008764", "fields": {"DriveType": {"official_value": "4WD/4-Wheel Drive/4x4", "fixed_value": "4x2"}}}]}
{"id": "rf-007", "release": "2026_11", "case": "wrong_value", "errors": [{"pattern": "4T3BA3BB*DU", "model_year": 2013, "make": "TOYOTA", "model": "Venza", "field": "DriveType", "vpic_value": "4x2", "correct_value": "AWD/4WD", "test_vehicles": 1}, {"pattern": "4T3ZA3BB*DU", "model_year": 2013, "make": "TOYOTA", "model": "Venza", "field": "DriveType", "vpic_value": "4WD/4-Wheel Drive/4x4", "correct_value": "FWD", "test_vehicles": 1}], "edits": [{"action": "modify", "table": "pattern", "row": {"id": 114068, "schema_id": 3433, "schema": "Toyota Schema for Venza MPV for 4T3-(2012-2013)", "keys": "B***B", "element": "DriveType", "attribute_id": "7", "value": "4x2"}, "set": {"attribute_id": "3", "value": "AWD/All-Wheel Drive"}}, {"action": "modify", "table": "pattern", "row": {"id": 114071, "schema_id": 3433, "schema": "Toyota Schema for Venza MPV for 4T3-(2012-2013)", "keys": "Z***B", "element": "DriveType", "attribute_id": "2", "value": "4WD/4-Wheel Drive/4x4"}, "set": {"attribute_id": "1", "value": "FWD/Front-Wheel Drive"}}], "reason": "The two Venza drive rows were swapped: B***B said 4x2 and Z***B 4WD, but NHTSA's 2013 Venza LE AWD test car has B and the Venza LE FWD has Z (Toyota uses B for 4WD and Z for 2WD in its other rows).", "evidence": [{"url": "https://nrd-static.nhtsa.dot.gov/reports/vehdb/v00000/v07900/v07969R001.pdf", "test_no": 7969}, {"url": "https://nrd-static.nhtsa.dot.gov/reports/vehdb/v00000/v07900/v07970R001.pdf", "test_no": 7970}], "reviewed": {"on": "2026-11-18", "by": "mcp.vin decode audit 2026-11-17 (confirmed list); rule rows traced by the local decoder"}, "checks": [{"vin": "4T3BA3BB8DU035697", "fields": {"DriveType": {"official_value": "4x2", "fixed_value": "AWD/All-Wheel Drive"}}}, {"vin": "4T3ZA3BB8DU064650", "fields": {"DriveType": {"official_value": "4WD/4-Wheel Drive/4x4", "fixed_value": "FWD/Front-Wheel Drive"}}}]}
{"id": "rf-008", "release": "2026_11", "case": "narrower_key", "errors": [{"pattern": "1V2BR2CA*JC", "model_year": 2018, "make": "VOLKSWAGEN", "model": "Atlas", "field": "DriveType", "vpic_value": "AWD/All-Wheel Drive", "correct_value": "FWD", "test_vehicles": 2}], "edits": [{"action": "add", "table": "pattern", "new": {"id": -103, "schema_id": 15825, "schema": "Volkswagen MPV Schema for WVG/1V2/3VV - 2018", "keys": "B**CA", "element": "DriveType", "attribute_id": "1", "value": "FWD/Front-Wheel Drive"}}], "premise": [{"table": "spec_pattern", "row": {"id": 14854, "spec_schema_pattern_id": 1710, "spec_schema_id": 439, "applies_to": "Atlas 2018, where Trim=Launch Model", "element": "DriveType", "attribute_id": "3", "value": "AWD/All-Wheel Drive"}}], "reason": "vPIC keys the 2018 Atlas drive on positions 4, 7 and 8 (G, H, K, L, M, N, R with CA: AWD) but has no row for B with CA, so the vehicle-spec value for 'Launch Model' (AWD) filled it. Volkswagen's own record of 1V2BR2CA3JC513174 reads 'ATLAS S 3.6 LAUNCH FWD' and both NHTSA test Atlases with B were front-drive; EPA lists FWD and 4Motion Atlases. A row B**CA now gives front-wheel drive.", "evidence": [{"url": "https://nrd-static.nhtsa.dot.gov/reports/vehdb/v10000/v10100/v10135R001.pdf", "test_no": 10135}, {"url": "https://nrd-static.nhtsa.dot.gov/reports/vehdb/v10000/v10100/v10136R001.pdf", "test_no": 10136}], "reviewed": {"on": "2026-11-18", "by": "mcp.vin decode audit 2026-11-17 (confirmed list); rule rows traced by the local decoder"}, "checks": [{"vin": "1V2BR2CA3JC513174", "fields": {"DriveType": {"official_value": "AWD/All-Wheel Drive", "fixed_value": "FWD/Front-Wheel Drive"}}}, {"vin": "1V2BR2CA9JC514037", "fields": {"DriveType": {"official_value": "AWD/All-Wheel Drive", "fixed_value": "FWD/Front-Wheel Drive"}}}]}
{"id": "rf-009", "release": "2026_11", "case": "wrong_value", "errors": [{"pattern": "19UUA9F5*CA", "model_year": 2012, "make": "ACURA", "model": "TL", "field": "DisplacementL", "vpic_value": "3.47406 L", "correct_value": "3.7 L", "test_vehicles": 2}], "edits": [{"action": "modify", "table": "pattern", "row": {"id": 848911, "schema_id": 9486, "schema": "Acura TL Schema for 2012", "keys": "UA9F[257]", "element": "DisplacementCI", "attribute_id": "212", "value": "212"}, "set": {"attribute_id": "224", "value": 224}}], "reason": "UA9F is the 2012 TL SH-AWD, whose engine vPIC itself names J37A4 (3.7 L); vPIC's own rows give that engine 224 cubic inches (UA9E5, and the RL's KB2F rows), but UA9F[257] said 212 (the 3.5 L), which converts to 3.47 L. Both NHTSA test TL SH-AWDs recorded 3.7 L.", "evidence": [{"url": "https://nrd-static.nhtsa.dot.gov/reports/vehdb/v00000/v07500/v07569R001.pdf", "test_no": 7569}, {"url": "https://nrd-static.nhtsa.dot.gov/reports/vehdb/v00000/v07800/v07869R001.pdf", "test_no": 7869}], "reviewed": {"on": "2026-11-18", "by": "mcp.vin decode audit 2026-11-17 (confirmed list); rule rows traced by the local decoder"}, "checks": [{"vin": "19UUA9F50CA003096", "fields": {"DisplacementCC": {"official_value": "3474.057568", "fixed_value": "3670.702336"}, "DisplacementCI": {"official_value": "212", "fixed_value": "224"}, "DisplacementL": {"official_value": "3.474057568", "fixed_value": "3.670702336"}}}, {"vin": "19UUA9F51CA010431", "fields": {"DisplacementCC": {"official_value": "3474.057568", "fixed_value": "3670.702336"}, "DisplacementCI": {"official_value": "212", "fixed_value": "224"}, "DisplacementL": {"official_value": "3.474057568", "fixed_value": "3.670702336"}}}]}
{"id": "rf-010", "release": "2026_11", "case": "wrong_row", "errors": [{"pattern": "1GCHTAEA*F1", "model_year": 2015, "make": "CHEVROLET", "model": "Colorado", "field": "EngineCylinders", "vpic_value": "6", "correct_value": "4", "test_vehicles": 1}], "edits": [{"action": "delete", "table": "pattern", "row": {"id": 1698453, "schema_id": 10453, "schema": "Chevrolet Colorado schema for 1GB/1GC - 2015", "keys": "*TA", "element": "EngineCylinders", "attribute_id": "6", "value": "6"}}], "reason": "The Colorado row *TA (positions 5-6) gave 6 cylinders whatever the engine; GM encodes the engine at position 8, where vPIC's own engine rows give A (LCV, 2.5 L) 4 cylinders. NHTSA's test Colorado with engine code A had 4 cylinders, and EPA lists no 2.5 L six. Removing the row lets the engine-code row decide.", "evidence": [{"url": "https://nrd-static.nhtsa.dot.gov/reports/vehdb/v00000/v09000/v09080R001.pdf", "test_no": 9080}], "reviewed": {"on": "2026-11-18", "by": "mcp.vin decode audit 2026-11-17 (confirmed list); rule rows traced by the local decoder"}, "checks": [{"vin": "1GCHTAEA5F1158421", "fields": {"EngineCylinders": {"official_value": "6", "fixed_value": "4"}}}]}
{"id": "rf-011", "release": "2026_11", "case": "wrong_value", "errors": [{"pattern": "WMWXM5C5*ET", "model_year": 2014, "make": "MINI", "model": "Hardtop", "field": "EngineCylinders", "vpic_value": "4", "correct_value": "3", "test_vehicles": 3}], "edits": [{"action": "modify", "table": "pattern", "row": {"id": 19118, "schema_id": 2452, "schema": "MINI Schema for WMW - 2014", "keys": "XM5C", "element": "EngineCylinders", "attribute_id": "4", "value": "4"}, "set": {"attribute_id": "3", "value": 3}}], "reason": "XM5C is the 2014 Cooper with the 1.5 L engine (vPIC's own displacement row for XM5C), which EPA lists only as a three-cylinder; the row said 4. All three NHTSA test cars with this pattern had 3 cylinders.", "evidence": [{"url": "https://nrd-static.nhtsa.dot.gov/reports/vehdb/v00000/v08700/v08755R001.pdf", "test_no": 8755}, {"url": "https://nrd-static.nhtsa.dot.gov/reports/vehdb/v00000/v08700/v08758R001.pdf", "test_no": 8758}, {"url": "https://nrd-static.nhtsa.dot.gov/reports/vehdb/v00000/v08700/v08786R001.pdf", "test_no": 8786}], "reviewed": {"on": "2026-11-18", "by": "mcp.vin decode audit 2026-11-17 (confirmed list); rule rows traced by the local decoder"}, "checks": [{"vin": "WMWXM5C53ET932798", "fields": {"EngineCylinders": {"official_value": "4", "fixed_value": "3"}}}, {"vin": "WMWXM5C59ET932711", "fields": {"EngineCylinders": {"official_value": "4", "fixed_value": "3"}}}, {"vin": "WMWXM5C51ET934114", "fields": {"EngineCylinders": {"official_value": "4", "fixed_value": "3"}}}]}
{"id": "rf-012", "release": "2026_11", "case": "wrong_value", "errors": [{"pattern": "3N1AB61E*7L", "model_year": 2007, "make": "NISSAN", "model": "Sentra", "field": "EngineCylinders", "vpic_value": "6", "correct_value": "4", "test_vehicles": 1}, {"pattern": "3N1AB61E*7L", "model_year": 2007, "make": "NISSAN", "model": "Sentra", "field": "DisplacementL", "vpic_value": "3.5 L", "correct_value": "2 L", "test_vehicles": 1}], "edits": [{"action": "modify", "table": "pattern", "row": {"id": 810114, "schema_id": 2662, "schema": "Nissan/Infiniti Passenger Car & Incomplete Vehicle Schema for JN1/1N4/3N1/JNK/JN3/JNX  - 2007", "keys": "AB61", "element": "EngineCylinders", "attribute_id": "6", "value": "6"}, "set": {"attribute_id": "4", "value": 4}}, {"action": "modify", "table": "pattern", "row": {"id": 45999, "schema_id": 2662, "schema": "Nissan/Infiniti Passenger Car & Incomplete Vehicle Schema for JN1/1N4/3N1/JNK/JN3/JNX  - 2007", "keys": "AB61", "element": "DisplacementL", "attribute_id": "3.5", "value": "3.5"}, "set": {"attribute_id": "2.0", "value": "2.0"}}], "reason": "The rows gave the 2007 Sentra pattern AB61 the 3.5 L VQ35DE six (vPIC's own rows give the other Sentra patterns BB61 and CB61 2.5 L). NHTSA's test Sentra had a 2.0 L four, and EPA lists no 3.5 L or six-cylinder 2007 Sentra. Not changed: the AB61 engine-model row (VQ35DE) is wrong too but was not in the reviewed list.", "evidence": [{"url": "https://nrd-static.nhtsa.dot.gov/reports/vehdb/v00000/v05800/v05876R001.pdf", "test_no": 5876}], "reviewed": {"on": "2026-11-18", "by": "mcp.vin decode audit 2026-11-17 (confirmed list); rule rows traced by the local decoder"}, "checks": [{"vin": "3N1AB61E97L600687", "fields": {"DisplacementCC": {"official_value": "3500.0", "fixed_value": "2000.0"}, "DisplacementCI": {"official_value": "213.58310433156", "fixed_value": "122.04748818946"}, "DisplacementL": {"official_value": "3.5", "fixed_value": "2.0"}, "EngineCylinders": {"official_value": "6", "fixed_value": "4"}}}]